 "result": "This is a Flask-style CLI, but the names are different here. Everything is in `src/tessel/cli.py`:\n\n- **Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` (`src/tessel/cli.py:380`). It's this repo's version of Flask's `with_appcontext`. If no app is active, it loads the app and runs your command inside `app.app_context()`.\n- **Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` (`src/tessel/cli.py:293`), through its `load_app()` method (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`). It's this repo's version of Flask's `ScriptInfo`. It tries `create_app` first, then `--app` / `TESSEL_APP`, then falls back to `wsgi.py` or `app.py`. To get it injected into a command, use `pass_script_info` (`src/tessel/cli.py:375`).\n\nYou may not need the decorator at all. Commands registered on `app.cli` or `bundle.cli`, or on any `AppGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`), are wrapped in `needs_app_scope` automatically. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to turn that off. You only need to apply the decorator yourself on a plain `click` command.",
